# Environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not,
# because it records which variables a deployment needs and no value in it is a
# secret.
#
# Nothing here is required to build or to develop. The site runs without either
# one; each only changes where the contact form delivers and where its booking
# buttons point.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMSPREE_FORM_ID
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where contact-form submissions are delivered by email.
#
# Create a form at https://formspree.io, then copy the id out of the endpoint URL
# it gives you -- `https://formspree.io/f/abcdwxyz` means `abcdwxyz`.
#
# Server-side only; deliberately NOT prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_, so it is never
# bundled into the browser. Set it in the Vercel project's environment variables
# for production.
#
# While it is unset, POST /api/contact answers 503 and tells the visitor to email
# instead. It does not pretend a submission succeeded.
FORMSPREE_FORM_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTACT_EMAIL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Overrides the address Formspree delivers to. Defaults to
# contact@adeelsayyad.tech, which is also the address the site publishes, so
# there is normally no reason to set this.
CONTACT_EMAIL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDAR_BOOKING_URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Google Calendar appointment-scheduling page that the "Let's Talk" buttons
# should open.
#
# Public, because it appears in an href. NEXT_PUBLIC_ means it is inlined into
# the browser bundle at build time -- changing it requires a rebuild, not just a
# restart.
#
# While it is unset the buttons fall back to /contact, which is where they
# already pointed, and `target="_blank"` is withheld so the same page does not
# open twice. No dead link ships in the meantime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDAR_BOOKING_URL=